{"_v":1,"id":"cymbeline-2007","bd":{"positive":1,"mixed":2,"negative":0},"rv":[{"cn":"THR Staff","o":"The Hollywood Reporter","s":62,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"http://www.hollywoodreporter.com/review/cymbeline-theater-review-813603","q":"Although entertaining in spots, this stylistically all-over-the-map rendition is more wearisome than enlightening"},{"cn":"Charles Isherwood","o":"The New York Times","s":62,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"http://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/11/theater/review-cymbeline-unspools-its-many-plot-twists-at-the-delacorte-theater.html","d":"2015-08-10","q":"The clarity and restrained opulence of the production are more satisfying, unfortunately, than the caliber of the performances, which tend toward blandness or overstatement."},{"cn":"Robert Kahn","o":"NBC New York","s":77,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"http://www.nbcnewyork.com/entertainment/the-scene/cymbeline-review-sitp-rabe-321255011.html%20","q":"Daffier than those of other period romances, its complex plot is kept comprehensible thanks to a sure-footed cast that includes Lily Rabe and Hamish Linklater as the put-upon lovers Imogen and Posthumus...The two share an on-stage chemistry that's clearly informed by their offstage relationship...Rabe's Imogen, here, is endearing...Linklater..."}],"au":{"score":81,"designation":"Liking","sources":{"ss":{"s":83,"c":32},"mz":{"s":76,"c":12,"sr":3.8}}},"ta":"150 W 65th St, New York, NY 10023","pd":"2007-11-01","ca":[{"n":"Jeffery M. Bender","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Daniel Breaker","r":"Gentleman"},{"n":"Jonathan Cake","r":"Iachimo"},{"n":"Michael Cerveris","r":"Posthumus Leonatus"},{"n":"Anthony Cochrane","r":"A Frenchman"},{"n":"John Cullum","r":"Cymbeline"},{"n":"Noshir Dalal","r":"A Spaniard"},{"n":"Adam Dannheisser","r":"Cloten"},{"n":"Jordan Dean","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Herb Foster","r":"Cornelius"},{"n":"David Furr","r":"Guiderius"},{"n":"Adam Greer","r":"The Ghost of Posthumus' Brother"},{"n":"Michael W. Howell","r":"Philarmonus"},{"n":"Ezra Knight","r":"Caius L